 succeeded in 0ms:
# BMH course Remotion boundary

For BMH course video production, do not use Remotion to animate standalone scene visuals. This has repeatedly produced off-brand results.

Hard rule:
- Remotion is allowed only for text pop-ins/code-rendered labels, logo/text overlays, and transitions between already-approved scenes.
- Remotion may animate between scenes, including camera-plane transitions when that style is approved.
- Remotion must not be used to create or animate the main content of a scene by itself.
- Scene visuals must come from the approved BMH visual pipeline/style and approved assets, not improvised code-drawn Remotion scenes.

When building or revising BMH course videos, treat any plan to make a full scene in Remotion as a scope error unless Jarrad explicitly approves that exception for that specific scene.

